  },
  {
    "episode_id": 83081,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83081.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 50,
    "turn_text": "In Denver, Colorado, the city tied its record all-time high of 105 degrees on June 28. A new world record was set in the Middle East last week. Along the coast of Oman, the temperature never dropped below 108.7 degrees over a 24-hour period. And in Glasgow, Scotland, the temperature reached a record-breaking 89.4 degrees on June 28th. That's more than 20 degrees hotter than its usual mild summer temperature.",
