    "turn_idx": 95,
    "turn_text": "Well, first we see, for example, studies in the city of Seattle that have implemented $15 minimum wage show that that is not the case. Secondly, one of the biggest problems that we have is 200 million Americans make less than $20,000 a year. That's 40% of this country. And how can we have an economy that grows? How can we build wealth as an economy if a large plurality of Americans are too poor to participate in it? Raising the minimum wage to a living wage will expand our economy. It will create wealth in our economy. And it will increase economic activity in this country. So for those that say it's unrealistic, this, that, and the other, it comes back to money and politics. Who's financing your campaign? And are the folks financing your campaign? Are the private equity groups financing your campaign? It's not a coincidence that they profit off of low wages.",
